      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would you explain a bit more about the issue? Does it stop building with meson?\n\nFrom the commit itself it looks like we should remove calling setLogger instead of making it no-op, unless if you hit a compile error.",
      "revId": "527ffa557c62b23cb051764e8c28aeae5130ce9a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3712303d_c154cddb",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101621
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-27T18:17:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It depends on a newer version of AEMU, I think.  For Linux-distro style package management, it\u0027s desirable for older versions of AEMU to still.  That means a newer gfxstream can work with an older AEMU.  \n\nSome details regarding AEMU versioning still have to be worked out (https://buganizer.corp.google.com/issues/300166662).\n\nAs for removing setLogger, I think it\u0027s mostly useful for AEMU.  QEMU/crosvm/others has it\u0027s own logging infrastructure.  So the idea is to keep API churn to the bare minimum necessary.",
      "parentUuid": "a4042c1f_a080442d",
      "revId": "527ffa557c62b23cb051764e8c28aeae5130ce9a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a858a14_b4f6a474",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1087303
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-27T18:44:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What would be the future plan? gfxstream has dependencies on aemu-base. Could we do something better than adding #ifdef for all new dependencies?",
      "parentUuid": "3712303d_c154cddb",
      "revId": "527ffa557c62b23cb051764e8c28aeae5130ce9a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "839b4719_7f813e6c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101621
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-27T22:33:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s an interesting question, and gets to https://buganizer.corp.google.com/issues/300166662.  Currently, the AEMU library exports the following shared or static libs:\n\n-`aemu-base`\n-`aemu-host-common`\n-`aemu-logging`\n-`aemu-snapshot`\n\n`aemu-logging` (at-least in gfxstream) could be deprecated possibly.  There are many loggers inside gfxstream itself: `ERR`, `FATAL`, `GL_LOG`, `VKDGS_LOG`.  We should really settle on one, and since we\u0027ve designed `stream_renderer_debug_callback` to hook into upstream QEMU/crosvm existent infra, that\u0027s a strong candidate for the gfxstream logging face.\n\nSimilarly, `aemu-snapshot` provides `TextureLoader.cpp` and `TextureSaver.cpp`.  However with VK coming up, from an API perspective it needs to change  (only images in Vulkan, not textures).  Additionally, `snapshot/include/snapshot/common.h` only includes headers, not implementations [`isSnapshotAlive`, `failureReasonToString`, `resetSnapshotLiveness` etc.].  The implementations probably live in the Android Emulator.  If we want a snapshot to work with upstream QEMU/crosvm, we probably need to think about the interface that needs to be exposed.  It seems QEMU/crosvm mostly works with snapshots, with the exception of GPU snapshots.  So we could think about just the gfxstream API for that.  Tracked with b/298208786.\n\nFor `host-common`, a lot of it seems to be video and goldfish-asg related.  For example, `MediaH264DecoderFfmpeg.cpp` and friends.  Not sure what the plan is for virtio-video in AEMU, but virtio-video is the crosvm/qemu plan.  So large parts of it could be deleted/moved into gfxstream.\n\nProbably aemu/base contains the most useful system abstractions.  We can probably keep some of those.\n\nSo I think most of AEMU depdencies can moved within gfxstream, and those that can\u0027t we can likely use some versioning mechanism.  It really depends a lot if there\u0027s a desire to use AEMU in upstream crosvm/qemu, independent of gfxstream.  If long-term it\u0027s gfxstream only, that defeats the purpose of a shared library somewhat.",
      "parentUuid": "0a858a14_b4f6a474",
      "revId": "527ffa557c62b23cb051764e8c28aeae5130ce9a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
